---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { PARTS, PEERS, ownsLabel } from "../data/landscape.js";

const organIds = PARTS.map((p) => p.id);
---

<BaseLayout>
  <header class="top">
    <span class="top-meta">lifeos · research · v0</span>
    <nav class="top-nav" aria-label="On this page">
      <a href="#scene">scene</a>
      <a href="#bundle">organs</a>
      <a href="#field">field</a>
      <a href="#lifeos">lifeos</a>
      <a href="#open">open</a>
      <a class="top-source" href="https://github.com/Angelguirao/meta-harness"
        >source</a
      >
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="brand">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1 id="brand" class="brand">meta-harness</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Working name for the shop above the coding agent — what survives when
          the chat dies.
        </p>
        <p class="dek">
          Not a pitch. Field notes from
          <a href="https://github.com/Angelguirao/personal-ai-os">LifeOS</a>
          against everyone shipping this layer.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-schematic" aria-hidden="true">
        <pre class="schematic"><code><span class="sch-shop">shop</span>  continuity · scope · constraint · work · retrieve · swap
  │
  ▼
<span class="sch-muscle">muscle</span>  claude code · codex · deep agents</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="scene" id="scene" aria-labelledby="scene-title">
      <h2 id="scene-title">Tuesday, still broken</h2>
      <p>
        Ticket: cancel a stuck order. Needs the payments API, the customer web
        app, and a design-system confirm dialog. Three repos. The coding agent
        edits one tree at a time. You clone, branch, paste context, babysit
        three PRs so they land in the same deploy.
      </p>
      <p>
        Last Thursday you already decided retries belong in the gateway — in a
        chat that is gone. The branch has the patch. Nothing queryable has the
        decision. Your other laptop burned the same afternoon yesterday.
      </p>
      <p class="punch">
        That gap is the category. Better prompts are not it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="define" id="define" aria-labelledby="define-title">
      <h2 id="define-title">Working definition</h2>
      <p>
        A <strong>harness</strong> is one agent loop in one session. A
        <strong>meta-harness</strong>, here, is not a SKU — it is a
        <strong>bundle of organs</strong> that make those loops usable across
        time, repos, and risk.
      </p>
      <p>
        Two different jobs share the name: <em>orchestration</em> (shop above
        the muscle) and <em>optimization</em> (outer loop that searches harness
        code — Stanford). This notebook is about the shop.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://metaharness.tools">metaharness.tools</a> maps the
        conversation. It is not our dictionary. We learn the label by placing
        LifeOS in the field.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="bundle" id="bundle" aria-labelledby="bundle-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="bundle-title">If this organ is missing</h2>
        <p>Failure modes — not feature slogans.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="matrix">
        {
          PARTS.map((part) => (
            <li>
              <span class="matrix-id">{part.label}</span>
              <span class="matrix-blurb">{part.miss}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="field" id="field" aria-labelledby="field-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="field-title">Field</h2>
        <p>Who owns which organ hard. Dot = center of gravity, not a score.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="coverage-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Organ coverage by peer">
        <table class="coverage">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col" class="coverage-name">Name</th>
              {
                PARTS.map((p) => (
                  <th scope="col">{p.label}</th>
                ))
              }
              <th scope="col" class="coverage-read">Read as</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              PEERS.map((p) => (
                <tr class:list={[{ "is-self": p.self }]}>
                  <th scope="row">
                    {p.url ? (
                      <a href={p.url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
                        {p.name}
                      </a>
                    ) : (
                      p.name
                    )}
                    <span class="sr-only"> owns {ownsLabel(p.organs)}</span>
                  </th>
                  {organIds.map((id) => (
                    <td>
                      {p.organs.includes(id) ? (
                        <span class="dot" title={id}>
                          ●
                        </span>
                      ) : (
                        <span class="dot-empty" aria-hidden="true">
                          ·
                        </span>
                      )}
                    </td>
                  ))}
                  <td class="coverage-note">{p.note}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="note">
        <mark>Cerebras Knowledge</mark> is retrieve done well. It can sit inside
        a fuller stack. Continuity, scope, and constraint are still someone
        else’s job — same as a tracker that only does work.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="lifeos" id="lifeos" aria-labelledby="lifeos-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="lifeos-title">LifeOS cut</h2>
        <p>What we actually run — not what we wish we shipped.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cut" role="group" aria-label="LifeOS inventory">
        <div class="cut-row">
          <span class="cut-k">heavy</span>
          <span class="cut-v"
            >World model (folio · ledger · trackers). OPEVL walker. Work / Run /
            Session as the coordination triad.</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="cut-row">
          <span class="cut-k">muscle</span>
          <span class="cut-v"
            >Fly Deep Agents today. Claude Code / Codex optional — swappable in
            doctrine, sticky in practice.</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="cut-row">
          <span class="cut-k">thin</span>
          <span class="cut-v"
            >Cross-repo scope. Session handoff agents can trust. OS-level
            sandbox.</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="cut-row cut-row-open">
          <span class="cut-k">bet</span>
          <span class="cut-v"
            >Harden a thin organ — or double down on the world model that
            dispatches wraps. Not both as the same product story.</span
          >
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="note">
        Thesis: control plane + world model first. Meta-harness organs attach
        under Session and Run. Not a rename. Not “we are Omnigent.”
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="open" id="open" aria-labelledby="open-title">
      <h2 id="open-title">Still open</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          After cancel-order lands across three repos, what is queryable next
          Tuesday without re-explaining the why?
        </li>
        <li>
          If we harden one thin organ next: handoff, sandbox, or scope?
        </li>
        <li>
          If Omnigent + Beads + a knowledge organ covered the week, would
          LifeOS still earn its keep — or is the world model the only
          irreplaceable piece?
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="foot">
    <p>
      Written beside LifeOS. Labels move. MIT ·
      <a href="https://github.com/Angelguirao/meta-harness">source</a>
    </p>
  </footer>

  <script>
    const links = [...document.querySelectorAll(".top-nav a[href^='#']")];
    const sections = links
      .map((a) => document.querySelector(a.getAttribute("href") || ""))
      .filter(Boolean);

    const sync = () => {
      const y = window.scrollY + 96;
      let current = sections[0];
      for (const s of sections) {
        if (s instanceof HTMLElement && s.offsetTop <= y) current = s;
      }
      links.forEach((a) => {
        a.classList.toggle(
          "is-active",
          current instanceof HTMLElement &&
            a.getAttribute("href") === `#${current.id}`,
        );
      });
    };

    sync();
    window.addEventListener("scroll", sync, { passive: true });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
